      "content": "I'm trying to wrap my head around the Fourier Transform for my signals class. I understand the integral formula, but I'm struggling with the physical intuition of the decomposition. When we transform a signal from the time domain to the frequency domain, what is actually happening to the information? How does the math \"isolate\" a specific frequency from a complex, noisy signal?",
